# The khold block service (services/khold/, .kiro/specs/khold-block-service/).
# Sourced from the top-level Kconfig's "Service Modules" menu.

config KHOLD
	bool "khold: Raft-replicated network block volumes for antikythera"
	default n
	help
	  Builds the services/khold/ module: a block service that stores
	  antikythera network volumes in Raft stripe groups and speaks hold
	  wire version 2 to antikythera's oar-blk initiator, running beside
	  antikythera's hold per volume class until it reaches feature and
	  testing parity. So far the module holds the khold_node placeholder
	  and the check that antikythera's wire formats, consumed through the
	  antikythera-proto overlay port, reproduce antikythera's test
	  vectors (task 1); the Raft append sink, witness voters and commit
	  predicates land in core, and the block store, stripe groups,
	  gateway and controller follow. Needs a C++ library with
	  std::expected (GCC 13+ or Clang 19+ over libstdc++); on Clang 18 the
	  build skips it. Off by default like every new module
	  (services/README.md). See .kiro/specs/khold-block-service/.
